<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sistine Madonna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1512–1513</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sistine Madonna is an oil painting by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raphael">Raphael</a>, made about 1512–1513 for the church of San Sisto in Piacenza. It shows the Virgin and Child on clouds between Pope Sixtus II and Saint Barbara, with two winged putti leaning on a ledge below. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustus-iii">Augustus III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> bought it in 1754 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>, where it hangs in the Old Masters Picture Gallery; taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1945, it was returned in 1955.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sistine-madonna.jpg" alt="Sistine Madonna" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raphael · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RAFAEL_-_Madonna_Sixtina_(Gem%C3%A4ldegalerie_Alter_Meister,_Dresden,_1513-14._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo,_265_x_196_cm).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
